# H37 — steel causal per-simdgroup mask-start (single file)

## One sentence
Raise the causal-mask loop entry from the threadgroup-wide first-row K-block
to each simdgroup's own first-row K-block so blocks fully below that
simdgroup's diagonal skip a pure no-op mask without changing any score.

## Diff envelope
- ONE file: Vendor/mlx-swift/Source/Cmlx/mlx-generated/steel_attention_nax.cpp
- +19 / -2
- JIT `_nax` twin only (runtime-effective on ranked M5)
- Not stacked with ratio-bound or GEMM_SWIZZLE

## Why bit-exact
Stock already elides K blocks fully ABOVE the diagonal via sg_kb_lim.
This only tightens the mask *start*: kb_min_causal used the threadgroup
first row; the simdgroup starts at tidl.x*BQ+tm, so kb < sg_kb_min_causal
⇒ every element satisfies col<=row. Skipping the mask loop on those sites
writes identical scores. Guard: do_causal && !has_mask (same as upper elision).

## Local correctness
Unverifiable on non-M5 (golden drift). Structural argument is the case.

## STOP STACKING
One file, one idea. Prefill steel attention only; decode SDPA vector untouched.


## Expanded argument
The stock steel attention nax kernel already derives a per-simdgroup upper
K-block limit (sg_kb_lim) so blocks fully above the causal diagonal skip
QK^T, softmax, and P@V. The mask *start* still used the threadgroup-wide
kb_min_causal = first_row_of_TG / BK. A simdgroup whose first row is
tidl.x*BQ + tm therefore re-runs the causal mask loop on K blocks that are
entirely below its diagonal — every (row,col) already satisfies col<=row, so
the mask writes nothing. Raising the entry to
sg_kb_min_causal = max(0, sg_q_min+1)/BK drops only those pure no-op
iterations. No float op order changes; no tile size changes; no load
coalescing changes.

## Why M5 and official have recently diverged
Recent single-file and multi-file submissions that measured positive on the
private M5 box have scored negative on the official runner. This candidate
is deliberately the smallest explainable work-removal on the JIT _nax path
that the ranked M5 actually executes. Local non-M5 numbers are discarded.

## Envelope
One editable path, under 400 lines, bit-exact by construction, no re-quant,
no input-token cache, no speculation. Ablation: the change is always-on
when do_causal&&!has_mask (same guard as the existing upper elision already
on tip); no env var needed because the skipped work is provably empty.

## Local correctness
Unverifiable on non-M5 (golden drift at step 0). Structural argument above.

